<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>BaZi Transit — {{.Name}} — {{.TransitDate}}</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem; background: #1a1a2e; color: #e0e0e0; }
    h1 { color: #e24a4a; border-bottom: 2px solid #e24a4a; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    h2 { color: #d23a3a; margin-top: 2rem; }
    .section { margin: 1.5rem 0; }
    .item { padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2a3e; }
    .planet { color: #e24a4a; font-weight: bold; }
    .aspect { color: #d23a3a; }
    .house { color: #7eb8da; }
    .orb { color: #888; font-size: 0.85em; }
    .note { color: #888; font-style: italic; margin: 1rem 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>BaZi Transit — {{.Name}}</h1>
  <div style="color:#888;font-size:0.9em">{{.TransitDate}}</div>

  <div class="note">BaZi transit analysis uses stem/branch relationships rather than degree-based aspects. The aspects below are computed from tropical longitudes for cross-system comparison.</div>

  <h2>Transit-to-Natal Aspects</h2>
  <div class="section">
    {{if .Aspects}}
    {{range .Aspects}}
    <div class="item">
      <span class="planet">{{.TransitPlanet}}</span>
      <span class="aspect">{{.Aspect}}</span>
      <span class="planet">{{.NatalPlanet}}</span>
      <span class="orb">(orb {{printf "%.1f" .Orb}}°)</span>
    </div>
    {{end}}
    {{else}}
    <div class="item">No significant transits at this orb.</div>
    {{end}}
  </div>

  <h2>Transit House Overlays</h2>
  <div class="section">
    {{range $planet, $house := .HouseOverlays}}
    <div class="item">
      <span class="planet">{{$planet}}</span> transiting
      <span class="house">{{$house}}{{ordinalSuffix $house}}</span>
    </div>
    {{end}}
  </div>
</body>
</html>
